{
  "$schema": "allos-dataset/v1",
  "id": "lifts",
  "title": "Curated strength-lift catalog",
  "description": "The strength catalog the activity logger, the pickers and every muscle-coverage surface read (issue #5175, moved verbatim out of lib/lifts.ts). `entries` are the STAND-ALONE lifts (one per movement) carrying the #482 MuscleId identity (primary/secondary), the coarse MuscleRegion each rolls up into, the push/pull/legs/core movement pattern, and the unilateral / timed / bodyweight / loadKind (#1922) load flags. `meta.variantGroups` are the base lifts that compose with an implement (\"Dumbbell Curl\"); the (equipment x base) PRODUCT is built in code by lib/datasets/lifts.ts, so the data declares the groups and the code declares the product. `meta.muscleRegions` / `meta.muscleLabels` are the MuscleId rollup and its display labels; `meta.defaultEquipment` is the best-effort implement a plain lift is normally performed with. Committed + HUMAN-REVIEWABLE, hand-curated (no generator). INFORMATIONAL exercise reference, NOT coaching or medical advice.",
  "citation": [
    {
      "source": "General resistance-training practice (curated, human-reviewable)",
      "url": "https://www.acsm.org",
      "note": "Lift selection, the prime-mover / assistor muscle tagging and the push/pull/legs/core patterns reflect general strength-training practice; the groupings are curated and human-reviewable, not coaching or medical advice."
    }
  ],
